Source, at 4cf3aed: wentOnFrom (session.go:704) reads the folder twice with no lock,
bindings() and then marks(). While another hook's carry turns the old id's binding into
a mark between the two readings, the old id is in both, so len(from) is 2.
tryMoveContinued (session.go:666) then returns blocked without taking the lock. Round 5
had no such early return: two candidates went on to the lock and were read again there.

